&lt;p&gt;We have around 650 engineers across Monzo who design and build our in-house banking platform. We have big ambitions for the future, and technology plays a big role in creating a bank our customers want, so engineers at Monzo collaborate across disciplines to solve interesting challenges throughout the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These range from the products our customers use everyday to underlying infrastructure, security, payments and finance, customer operations, financial crime, and data, to name just a few areas. As a bank, there is scope for impact across a huge number of opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We contribute to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/monzo&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;open source software&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; as much as possible. Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/technology&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;blog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;is a good place to learn even more about what we do!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your day-to-day&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is all about collaborating with your team to make a difference to your customers. As a backend engineer you’ll work in a squad alongside other disciplines like product managers, marketers, user researchers, designers, mobile engineers, web engineers, data analysts, business analysts, writers and more!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together you&#39;ll build and support a particular part of Monzo. Our squads belong to our wider collectives (a word we use to describe self-governing business units of ~100 people). They are: Core Banking, Business Banking, Wealth, Borrowing, Growth, Payments, Platform, Fincrime, Security &amp;amp; Expansion. All of our collectives are doing innovative work, many of which have machine learning and AI at the forefront- from fighting financial crime to building smarter financial tools - and you may have the opportunity to join a collective that gives you direct exposure to this exciting space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They’re all looking for additional Backend Engineers right now, we do a standard interview process across all our collectives and at the end we will find the best match for you based on your skills, experience, preferences and aligning with the business need!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our backend engineers have a variety of different backgrounds. As long as you enjoy learning new things, we’d love to talk to you. We do not ask for formal qualifica

&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cambridge Consultants, we believe the future of technology isn&#39;t just smart, it has agency. We&#39;re moving past passive tools and building human-centred digital services and products: systems that reason, plan, and act around the people who use them. Our work spans autonomous systems at the frontier of biology, sensing, and AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We hire self-motivated builders, not ticket-takers. If you thrive in highly agile environments, can cut through ambiguity with first-principles thinking, and want to ship things that matter, this is the kind of place where you&#39;ll feel at home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be working on systems that haven&#39;t existed before. Think of an Agentic Coach that navigates the unpredictability of human biology, or the software architecture behind a fully automated Dark Lab. These aren&#39;t chatbots waiting for questions. They&#39;re proactive systems that maintain world models, interpret human intent, and intervene before the user knows to ask. These systems create genuine impact for clients tackling problems no one else can solve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building them means designing and wiring agent harnesses: layered architectures that span from sensor-edge reasoning to high-level planning, backed by stateful multi-turn reasoning, persistent per-user memory, and robust evaluation pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work in two directions at once. Internally, you&#39;ll use the latest AI tools to sharpen how we build, prototype, and ship. Externally, you&#39;ll deliver the breakthrough systems our clients deploy, designed to move from prototype to production at pace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There&#39;s no single technology stack. You&#39;ll work with agents, multi-agent systems, and the latest generative AI tools, but your work will always be grounded in solid software engineering. Expect to build scalable distributed systems in core languages like Python and TypeScript, leveraging frameworks such as NextJS and Pydantic, agent orchestration tools (LangGraph, CrewAI), and protocols like MCP. You&#39;ll deploy on cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure) using Docker, Kubernetes, and infrastructure-as-code, backed by rigorous CI/CD and observability (OpenTelemetry, Prometheus).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the clients we work with, you must be eligible for UK security clearance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we ask of you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The examples below describe the core domains our AI Engineers own within the Digital Services team. We don&#39;t expect every candidate to have mastered all of these, but if you can demonstrate a strong combination of the following, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI System Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Designing and implementing the logic for autonomous systems, including maintaining world models, integrating multimodal sensing, and building real-time human-machine interact

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes Cloudbeds Unique&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Cloudbeds, we&#39;re not just building software, we’re transforming hospitality. Our intelligently designed platform powers properties across 150 countries, processing billions in bookings annually. From independent properties to hotel groups, we help hoteliers transform operations and uplevel their commercial strategy through a unified platform that integrates with hundreds of partners. And we do it with a completely remote team. Imagine working alongside global innovators to build AI-powered solutions that solve hoteliers&#39; biggest challenges. Since our founding in 2012, we&#39;ve become the World&#39;s Best Hotel PMS Solutions Provider and landed on Deloitte&#39;s Technology Fast 500 again in 2024, but we&#39;re just getting started.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Locatio&lt;/strong&gt;n: Remote in Europe&lt;/p&gt;
